    vela_builder_add(v_out, VELA_STR("A top-level `test \"description\" { ... }` uses `assert(condition)`. Fakes isolate effects with `with files = [\"data.txt\": \"contents\"] { ... }`, `with args = [\"program\", \"arg\"] { ... }`, `with env = [\"KEY\": \"value\"] { ... }`, and `with stdin = \"input\\n\" { ... }`. Capture output with `let mut out: [Str] = []` and `with stdout = mut out { ... }`. Use `with clock = [wall_ns, mono_ns]`, `with net = [net.reply(host, port, expected_write, response)]`, and `with processes = [processes.reply(args, input, status, stdout, stderr)]`. Transcript rows are consumed once; unmatched requests fail and unconsumed expectations panic. Socket copies alias a connection; close rejects new operations, final release closes it. Running operations finish or time out. Unicode helpers validate UTF-8/scalars; io interfaces return next state; http supports plaintext HTTP/1.1 GET. Timeouts bound socket waits (DNS resolution uses the host resolver). Fakes are restored on every exit. Library tests run through vela test. Check formatting and warnings.\012", 1031));
